 Minutes\nSustainability Initiatives\nResearch\nOpportunities\nScholarships\nResearch Groups\nAnimal Physiology\nCell and Molecular Biology\nEcology, Evolution and Behaviour\nEnvironmental Studies\nFisheries and Aquatics\nMathematical Biology\nPEARL\nPlant Sciences\nQuantitative Skills Group\nDepartmental Seminars\nWeekly Seminars\nThe Aylward E.R. Downe Annual Memorial Lecture\nBiology Capstone Annual Seminar\nQUIP\nSWEP\nJob Board\nEmployment Opportunities\nAvailable Positions\nEDII\nOutreach\nWellness\nContact\nPayment\nBreadcrumb\nHome\nProspective Students\nGraduate Students\nHow to Apply\nHow to Apply\nApply Now\nInterested in doing an MSc or PhD in the Biology Department? Your best bet is to contact a professor who you think might be a suitable supervisor for the sort of research that interests you. Applications made through the School of Graduate Studies, without first contacting a potential supervisor, are almost never successful.\nOnline Application for MSc and PhD Programs\u2014on-line forms provided by the Graduate School\nOGS application deadline: March 8, 2027\nBiology Canadian and International student application deadline: February 8, 2027\nAll documents (reference letters, transcripts, IELTS scores, must be submitted by this deadline to be considered for recruitment awards)\nGraduate Studies Admission Application\nMost professors receive many applications each year so the majority are turned down. Overall we usually accept about 20 new MSc students, and 10 new PhD students each academic year. To initiate the application process, we suggest you send an email to potential supervisors, outlining your interests, skill, and relevant background. Do not make a formal application until at least one professor expresses strong interest in taking you on as a graduate student.\nThe Department of Biology at Queen\u2019s University is committed to providing the best in graduate learning and research mentorship while striving for an inclusive and supportive environment.\nWe welcome graduate students from all backgrounds acknowledging that a diversity of perspectives, experiences, and voices contributes to a healthy and vibrant department.\nWe uphold non-discrimination on the basis of race, ethnicity, religion, sex, age, national origin, ability, sexual orientation, gender identity, and gender expression. We are committed to identifying, understanding, and removing barriers to equal opportunities for all students and other members of the department.\nThe following are inclusivity statements from:\nFaculty of Arts and Science\nSchool of Graduate Studies (See 1. Equity Admissions Regulation and 2. Information for Indigenous Students.)\nFunding opportunities are available for Indigenous students (note: the Robert Sutherland fellowships are available to incoming Aboriginal students, African Canadian students and other Canadian visible minority students).\nIf you have questions about departmental functioning or atmosphere and would like to ask a current graduate student, please contact the co-chairs of the Biology Graduate Student Council (BGSC).\nPlease note that admission applications are also used to in adjudication of Ontario Graduate Scholarships and internal (Queen\u2019s) awards, so it is important to:\nWrite a strong Statement of Interest,\nInclude as much information as possible under Previous Awards and Publications (including any papers that have been submitted to peer review but not yet accepted, conference presentations, popular articles, etc),\nAsk your referees to write strong letters, including academic achievements as well as leadership and outreach activities.\nDepartment of Biology, Queen's University\nBiosciences Complex\n116 Barrie St.\nKingston ON K7L 3N6\nCanada\nTelephone\n(613) 533-6160\nUndergraduate\nTelephone\n(613) 533-6344\nEmail\nug.biology@queensu.ca\nGraduate\nTelephone\n(613) 533-6138\nEmail\nbiologygradassistant@queensu.ca\nQueen's University is situated on traditional Haudenosaunee and Anishinaabe territory.\n\u00a9 2026 Department of Biology, Queen's University. All Rights Reserved.\nNews\nSite Map\nDonate\nWebsite Privacy\nLog in", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://biology.queensu.ca/prospective-students/graduate-students/how-to-apply#main"], ["", "https://www.queensu.ca/"], ["Sign In", "https://biology.queensu.ca/prospective-students/graduate-students/how-to-apply"], ["", "https://biology.queensu.ca/prospective-students/graduate-students/how-to-apply"], ["Department of Biology , Queen's University", "https://biology.queensu.ca/"], ["Donate", "https://biology.queensu.ca/donate"], ["Home", "https://biology.queensu.ca/"], ["Prospective Students", "https://biology.queensu.ca/prospective-students"], ["Mission Statement", "https://biology.queensu.ca/prospective-students/mission-statement"], ["Our Vision", "https://biology.queensu.ca/prospective-students/mission-statement/our-vision"], ["Uniquely Queen's Biology", "https://biology.queensu.ca/prospective-students/uniquely-queens-biology"], ["Undergraduate Students", "https://biology.queensu.ca/prospective-students/undergraduate-students"], ["Student Community", "https://biology.queensu.ca/prospective-students/undergraduate-students/student-community"], ["Admission Requirements", "https://biology.queensu.ca/prospective-students/undergraduate-students/admission-requirements"], ["Fees and Funding", "https://biology.queensu.ca/prospective-students/undergraduate-students/fees-and-funding"], ["How to Apply", "https://biology.queensu.ca/prospective-students/undergraduate-students/how-to-apply"], ["Degree Plans", "https://biology.queensu.ca/current-students/undergraduate-students/department-student-council"], ["Careers and Alumni", "https://biology.queensu.ca/prospective-students/undergraduate-students/careers-and-alumni"], ["Student Resources", "https://biology.queensu.ca/prospective-students/undergraduate-students/student-resources"], ["Contacts", "https://biology.queensu.ca/prospective-students/undergradua